From d296c67def1ac01e6879f3a9b9a0cf8dc1a421ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gavin_darkglider <rbrown4014@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:17:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 03/13] core: draw the splash with the framebuffer console's
 rotation

Make splashutils work on rotated consoles (fbcon=rotate:N, the fbcon
rotate/rotate_all sysfs knobs), e.g. portrait panels used in landscape.

- New fbsplash_get_rotation(): splash=rotate:N if given, otherwise the
  current fbcon rotation from /sys/class/graphics/fbcon/rotate, otherwise
  fbcon=rotate:N from the kernel command line.  Stored as config.rotate,
  appended to fbspl_cfg_t (libfbsplash interface age bumped).
- struct fb_data gains the rotation and the logical (rotated) resolution.
  Theme selection (<w>x<h>.cfg), margins, text-box sanitizing and the
  verbose picture all use the logical resolution, which is what the
  rotation-aware fbcondecor kernel interface expects: the kernel lays the
  picture out itself.
- The silent splash is drawn by a single rotation-aware blitter used by
  put_img(), paint_rect() and the fades, mapping logical to physical
  pixels exactly like fbcon (fbcon_cw.c & co.) and writing the
  framebuffer in physical row order.
- fade_truecolor() now renders each step into a buffer and blits it,
  which also fixes its 24bpp reads past the end of the image.
- fbsplashr_tty_silent_update() requests a theme reload when only the
  rotation changed.
- Text boxes are clamped so tx+tw/ty+th fit the screen (the kernel
  rejects anything else).
- Fix an out-of-bounds write on an empty /proc/cmdline and a wrong
  bounds check while parsing BOOT_MSG.
- New unit test checking the blitter against fbcon's mapping for all
  rotations at 16/24/32bpp.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
